{{also|Heathen}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hethen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hǣþen}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*haiþinaz}}; akin to {{m|en|heath|t=heathland}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|heiden}}, {{cog|de|Heide}}, {{cog|da|hedning}}, {{cog|nn|heidning}}, {{cog|is|heiðingi}}. See also Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*haiduz}}, Old Norse {{m|non|heiðr|tr=honour, bright, moor}}, Icelandic {{m|is|heiður|tr=honour}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhiːðən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-heathen.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːðən}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Not adhering to [[Christian]] [[religion]]; [[pagan]].
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Uncultured; uncivilized; savage, [[philistine]].
# {{alternative case form of|en|Heathen|nodot=1}} {{gloss|pertaining or adhering to the Germanic [[neo-pagan]] faith [[Heathenry]]}}.

